TOOL STATES

The tool must support these states:

1. Empty
   - Input is empty.
   - All counters display 0.
   - Clear button is disabled.
   - Copy button is disabled.

2. Active / Typing
   - User is entering or editing text.
   - Statistics update in real time.

3. Has Content
   - Valid text exists.
   - Copy and Clear actions are available.

4. Copied
   - After successful copying, provide a short accessible confirmation:
     "Text copied."
   - Do not use an intrusive modal.

5. Error / Unsupported
   - If an operation fails, display a concise human-readable error.
   - The rest of the tool must remain functional.
##*
UNICODE AND MULTILINGUAL COUNTING

The tool must use Unicode-aware JavaScript text processing.

It must work with:
- English
- Bengali
- Arabic
- Hindi
- Chinese
- Japanese
- Korean
- accented Latin characters
- emoji
- mixed-language text

Word counting must not depend on ASCII-only regular expressions.

Character counting must distinguish:
- Characters including spaces
- Characters excluding spaces

The implementation should use Unicode-aware APIs where appropriate,
such as Intl.Segmenter when supported, with a sensible fallback.

Do not incorrectly split surrogate pairs or common Unicode characters.
##*
CLIPBOARD REQUIREMENT

Primary method:
navigator.clipboard.writeText()

Fallback:
Provide a compatibility fallback for browsers where the Clipboard API
is unavailable or fails.

The tool must not become unusable simply because clipboard permission
is unavailable.

After success:
Announce "Text copied."

After failure:
Show a concise accessible message explaining that automatic copying
was unavailable.
##*
ACCESSIBLE LIVE-REGION BEHAVIOR

Do not make the entire statistics area continuously assertive.

Real-time counters should update visually without causing excessive
screen-reader announcements on every keystroke.

Use aria-live="polite" only for meaningful status messages where
appropriate.

Examples:
- "Text copied."
- "Text cleared."

Do not continuously announce:
"1 word, 2 words, 3 words, 4 words..."
while the user types.
